, and audit evidence is reconciled.\nA successful mechanical check is not health authority or closure authority. Emergency procurement does not waive water-quality, accessibility, labor, privacy, evidence-custody, or independent-review obligations.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiver acknowledges the same operating map, facility roster, current demand model, communications release, and candidate version. Version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCLIMATE supplies hazard thresholds, GRID and WATER supply infrastructure state, and REVIEW supplies independent findings; none may authorize closure.\nLINEAGE binds the current candidate while COUNCIL separates activation, limited operations, expanded operations, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v3 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-office | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-desk | v3 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-liaison | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-office | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-desk | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-liaison | v3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | health-office | v3 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | utility-desk | v3 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-liaison | v3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v3 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | health-office | v4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | utility-desk | v4 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | public-liaison | v4 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-command | v4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | health-office | v4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-0