inst a twelve-minute ceiling. The p95 observation is not a population average or readiness percentage.\nA bed closure, staffing change, triage protocol, ambulance roster, reporting method, or candidate facility change makes prior clinical evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nLABOR supplies licensed coverage, GRID and WATER constrain facilities, and TRANSIT supplies accessible transport alternatives.\nCOUNCIL authorizes public states while REVIEW independently reconciles current clinical blockers.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CLN-000 | hospital-a | v3 | 71.0 | percent-occupied | superseded |\n| CLN-001 | hospital-b | v3 | 72.7 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-002 | urgent-care | v3 | 71.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-003 | ambulance-post | v3 | 73.2 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-004 | hospital-a | v3 | 72.0 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-005 | hospital-b | v3 | 73.7 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-006 | urgent-care | v3 | 72.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-007 | ambulance-post | v3 | 71.3 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-008 | hospital-a | v3 | 73.0 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-009 | hospital-b | v3 | 71.8 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-010 | urgent-care | v3 | 73.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-011 | ambulance-post | v3 | 72.3 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-012 | hospital-a | v3 | 71.1 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-013 | hospital-b | v4 | 72.8 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-014 | urgent-care | v4 | 71.6 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-015 | ambulance-post | v4 | 73.3 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-016 | hospital-a | v4 | 72.1 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-017 | hospital-b | v4 | 73.8 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-018 | urgent-care | v4 | 72.6 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-019 | ambulance-post | v4 | 71.4 | percent-occupied | current |\